From 2628b56892b79ae35c1ace0ec481f469d0c0eebc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 23:16:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quick-match): harden MonoQuickMatch UX & a11y (safe
 items, #106)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The independent, low-risk items from the #106 audit:
- Discard now requires confirmation (ConfirmDialog) instead of silently wiping an
  in-progress match. EndMatchDialog generalized to ConfirmDialog (defaults
  reproduce the End-match copy/ids byte-for-byte; distinct idPrefix avoids dup ids).
- Per-action feedback: ScoringStatusStrip (an aria-live region that was defined but
  never rendered) now mounts in all three scorer branches so every action is
  announced and shown.
- Autosave no longer re-serializes the whole draft every second: timer.elapsed
  dropped from the effect deps (startedAt persists; elapsed is reconstructed on
  restore).
- Sets "win by N" label derives from getSetWinRule (config/customization) instead
  of a hardcoded 2.
- Start button stays focusable + aria-disabled with linked guidance instead of a
  hard-disabled, opacity-dimmed control (startMatch already self-guards).
- Goals half no longer uses the disabled-button antipattern when quick buttons own
  scoring — renders a non-interactive display so the score stays in the a11y tree.
- Team autocomplete shows "Searching…" (query in-flight) and an explicit empty
  state instead of silently rendering nothing.

Cricket innings-transition refactor, timed-goals end, innings-break, and the live-
bar layout slot follow in separate commits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
